  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Much needed/second chance rainfall opportunity \nfor the Lower Susquehanna Valley early today \n\nSlower-to-exit cold front (thanks to trailing/developing sfc \nlow pressure wave from eastern VA to southern portions of the \nDelMarVa) will provide another opportunity/second chance for \nmuch needed rainfall across the southeastern portion of the \nforecast area early today with the main focus over the Lower \nSusquehanna Valley (LSV) particularly southeast of I-81. PWs\nwill still be quite high this morning, so we can't rule out a \ncouple of localized heavy thunderstorms/downpours. Showers \nshould exit the southeastern zones by this evening with clearing\nskies and pleasant conditions (lower humidity) for Wednesday. \n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Increasing heat risk to end June and start July \n\nA major pattern change over the Pacific Northwest and \nIntermountain West this weekend will likely result in a \ndownstream upper ridge developing over the eastern U.S. by early\nnext week. Blended ensemble guidance driving the prototype\nprobabilistic heatrisk is confirming the signal for a building \nto potentially prolonged heatwave to end June and start July.\nCPC has placed a 20-40% slight risk of extreme heat over CPA\nfrom 6/30-7/6 with higher chances in the 40-60% range in\nsoutheast PA. High humidity and temperatures (highs in the 90s\nwith heat index values possibly reaching 100F) will greatly \nincrease the risk of heat-related illness.",
